---
# A session nobody touches any more (the turn over, both acks saved, B
# caught up) has no next step; that is an end state, not a deadlock. The
# liveness checks still see it: an end state stutters forever.
deadlock_detection: false
---
# Two browser tabs on one session (go/tests/model/README.md). Tab A is
# the one acting: it archives, unarchives, renames, stops or marks the
# session seen. Tab B has the same session open and only learns about A
# through its list poll or the session's event stream, and it may act on
# what it last read.
#
# Server (go/internal/serve): POST /archive and /unarchive set
# meta.Archived (SetArchived kills the child when archiving; both are
# idempotent: a second archive answers 200), /rename sets the title in
# meta, /interrupt stops the turn, /ack is Supervisor.Acknowledge, and
# /prompt refuses an archived session with 409 (ErrArchived). The row's
# unseen is "the last done is past meta.Ack" (digest.go).
#
# Page (web/src/app.tsx): the list poll (refresh(true)) runs every 4 s,
# every 12 s while a session is open (its event stream is expected to
# carry its changes), never in a hidden tab, and once at once when the
# tab comes back. It reads the open session's row too, also when the
# list no longer has it (archived). Every action of B's goes through act
# or deliverTo, whose finally awaits refresh(): B's own action ends with
# a fresh read. archiveRow picks Archive or Unarchive from B's copy of
# the row (r.archived), not the server's. The page acks a shown unseen
# finish (viewingUnseen) unless document.hidden, and refreshes after.
#
# Fields: the server's (archived, title, status, seq, ack, unseen), B's
# copy of the row (bArchived, bTitle, bStatus, bUnseen), B's tab
# (bVisible), whether B has read since the server last changed (bFresh),
# whether B's composer shows a refused send (bRefused: set by the Send
# that was refused, gone at B's next read) and the two acks in flight (aAck, bAck: -1 when none, else the seq the ack read).
#
# Mapped states, as field values:
#   BothViewing              bFresh and bVisible
#   AArchived_BStale         archived and not bArchived
#   BPollDropsRow/BShowsArchived  a PollTick after that: bArchived
#   ARenamed_BHeaderStale    title != bTitle
#   AStopped_BWorking        status "stopped", bStatus "working"
#   AAcked_BDotStale         not unseen and bUnseen
#   BHidden / BVisibleAgain  bVisible False / True again
#   BActsOnStale             B.ArchiveMenu or B.Send with bFresh False
#   AckRead_n_then_saved_after_n+1  aAck or bAck < seq while saving
#   UnseenAgainSpurious      unreachable: the ack is saved as max(); see
#                            AckMonotonic
#   Converged                bFresh, no ack in flight, nothing unseen
#
# Where this differs from the code, on purpose or as a finding:
# - Supervisor.Acknowledge reads the entries without s.mu and then sets
#   meta.Ack unconditionally. Two acks that race a new entry can save out
#   of order: the one that read seq n saves after the one that read n+1,
#   meta.Ack goes back to n and the finish at n+1 shows unseen again,
#   in both tabs, although B already acked it. The spec saves
#   max(ack, read) (AckSave), which is the contract AckMonotonic and
#   NoSpuriousUnseen state; the code's unconditional set fails both (the
#   mutation that proves them is exactly the code).
# - seq counts done entries only, at most MAXSEQ. A stopped turn writes
#   an interrupted done in the product; it never makes the row unseen
#   (status is not done), so here it writes nothing.
# - Archiving kills the child: a turn in flight ends "stopped".
# - The event stream carries status only (a turn ending, an interrupt);
#   rename and archive reach B by the poll. An archived session has no
#   child and sends no event (Event requires not archived).
# - A's own view is always fresh (every action of A's refreshes) and is
#   not state here; A's Archive/Unarchive/Rename/Stop are single
#   requests, atomic steps. Only A's ack is split, to race B's.
# - The palette's "Mark every failure seen" acks through the same
#   Acknowledge; it is A.AckRead/AckSave here (trouble is not modelled).
# - One rename, t0 -> t1, before the first turn. A rename is a meta write
#   that touches nothing else here; its only interplay is B's copy going
#   stale, which one rename shows. Renaming later, or again, multiplies
#   every ack interleaving by the title and adds no claim (~1.5x states).
# - Timing is not modelled: "within one poll" is "at the next PollTick";
#   that B waits 12 s instead of 4 s while streaming is a latency, not a
#   state.

MAXSEQ = 2

role Session:
    action Init:
        self.archived = False
        self.title = "t0"
        self.status = "idle"
        self.seq = 0
        self.ack = 0
        self.unseen = False
        self.bArchived = False
        self.bTitle = "t0"
        self.bStatus = "idle"
        self.bUnseen = False
        self.bVisible = True
        self.bFresh = True
        self.bRefused = False
        self.aAck = -1
        self.bAck = -1

    # Any change on the server: the row's unseen is derived again, and
    # B's copy is no longer known to be current.
    atomic func changed():
        self.unseen = self.status == "done" and self.seq > self.ack
        self.bFresh = False

    # B's refresh: the list read (or the open row's own read, once the
    # list no longer has it) replaces B's copy of the row.
    atomic func bRead():
        self.bArchived = self.archived
        self.bTitle = self.title
        self.bStatus = self.status
        self.bUnseen = self.unseen
        self.bFresh = True
        self.bRefused = False

    # --- tab A: one request each, A's view refreshed after ---

    atomic action AArchive:
        require not self.archived
        self.archived = True
        if self.status == "working":
            self.status = "stopped"
        self.changed()

    atomic action AUnarchive:
        require self.archived
        self.archived = False
        self.changed()

    atomic action ARename:
        require self.title == "t0" and self.seq == 0 and self.status == "idle"
        self.title = "t1"
        self.changed()

    atomic action AStop:
        require self.status == "working"
        self.status = "stopped"
        self.changed()

    # Acknowledge, split where the code is: the entries are read first
    # (outside s.mu), the ack saved later under it. A marks seen only
    # what it shows as unseen.
    atomic action AAckRead:
        require self.unseen and self.aAck == -1
        self.aAck = self.seq

    atomic fair action AAckSave:
        require self.aAck != -1
        if self.aAck > self.ack:
            self.ack = self.aAck
        self.aAck = -1
        self.changed()

    # --- the session's child ---

    # The turn finishes: a done entry, the row unseen until acked.
    atomic fair action ChildWritesEntry:
        require self.status == "working"
        self.seq = self.seq + 1
        self.status = "done"
        self.changed()

    # --- tab B ---

    # The list poll (or the read on coming back to the tab). Only when it
    # has something to bring: a read that changes nothing is not a step.
    atomic fair<strong> action BPollTick:
        require self.bVisible and not self.bFresh
        self.bRead()

    # The session's event stream: a status change, not a row. Events
    # arrive in a hidden tab too (EventSource keeps running).
    atomic action BEvent:
        require not self.archived and self.bStatus != self.status
        self.bStatus = self.status

    atomic action BHide:
        require self.bVisible
        self.bVisible = False

    atomic action BShow:
        require not self.bVisible
        self.bVisible = True

    # archiveRow on B's copy: Unarchive when B thinks it archived, else
    # Archive (after the confirm dialog). Both requests are idempotent on
    # the server, so a stale B re-archives or re-unarchives harmlessly;
    # act's refresh then brings B's copy up to date.
    atomic action BArchiveMenu:
        require self.bVisible
        if self.bArchived:
            if self.archived:
                self.archived = False
                self.changed()
        else:
            if not self.archived:
                self.archived = True
                if self.status == "working":
                    self.status = "stopped"
                self.changed()
        self.bRead()

    # The composer: disabled while B's copy says archived or working
    # (a running turn gets a steer, which is not this flow). A stale copy
    # sends to an archived session: serve answers 409 and deliverTo shows
    # the message. Otherwise a turn starts. Bounded by MAXSEQ turns.
    atomic action BSend:
        require self.bVisible and not self.bArchived and self.bStatus != "working" and self.seq < MAXSEQ
        refused = self.archived
        if not self.archived:
            self.status = "working"
            self.changed()
        self.bRead()
        self.bRefused = refused

    # viewingUnseen: B shows the transcript, its copy says unseen, and
    # the tab is not hidden. The ack's save refreshes B.
    atomic fair<strong> action BAckRead:
        require self.bVisible and self.bUnseen and self.bAck == -1
        self.bAck = self.seq

    atomic fair action BAckSave:
        require self.bAck != -1
        if self.bAck > self.ack:
            self.ack = self.bAck
        self.bAck = -1
        self.changed()
        self.bRead()

action Init:
    session = Session()

# The menu B offers is "Archive" exactly when its copy says not archived:
# once B has read the row, that copy is the server's.
always assertion NoArchiveOfferOnceRead:
    return not (session.bFresh and session.archived and not session.bArchived)

# B's header (title, status, dot) equals the server's after one read.
always assertion BReadIsTruth:
    s = session
    return not s.bFresh or (s.bArchived == s.archived and s.bTitle == s.title and
                            s.bStatus == s.status and s.bUnseen == s.unseen)

# An archived session never runs a turn: nothing B sends starts one.
always assertion ArchivedNeverWorks:
    return not (session.archived and session.status == "working")

# B's send to an archived session is refused with a message, never
# delivered and never unarchiving it on the quiet.
# (ArchivedNeverWorks covers "never delivered".)
transition assertion ArchivedSendRefused(before, after):
    b = before.session
    a = after.session
    if not b.bRefused and a.bRefused:
        return a.archived and b.archived and a.status == b.status
    return True

# A hidden tab never starts an ack.
transition assertion HiddenTabNeverAcks(before, after):
    return before.session.bVisible or not (before.session.bAck == -1 and after.session.bAck != -1)

# meta.Ack never goes back.
transition assertion AckMonotonic(before, after):
    return after.session.ack >= before.session.ack

# A finish that was seen does not come back unseen without a new entry.
transition assertion NoSpuriousUnseen(before, after):
    b = before.session
    a = after.session
    return not (not b.unseen and a.unseen) or a.seq > b.seq

# B converges once visible: its copy is current again, and stays so
# until the server next changes.
always eventually assertion BConverges:
    return not session.bVisible or session.bFresh

# Viewing a session clears its unseen in every tab: the server's dot and
# B's copy of it.
always eventually assertion UnseenClears:
    return not session.bVisible or not (session.unseen or session.bUnseen)
